{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ef3mqijqvYAMNr9qdoeUZn","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Scenario Builder — Visual & UI Test Scenarios\n2\t\n3\t## Scope\n4\tBuild test scenarios for the visual demo app based on gaps identified in the visual audit.\n5\t\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t## Priority 1 — Bug: IDA* heuristic reads wrong radio group\n9\t\n10\t**File:** `visual/js/panel.js:160`\n11\t**Bug:** Reads `input[name=jump_point_heuristic]` instead of `input[name=ida_heuristic]`\n12\t**Scenario:** Select IDA*, pick Euclidean in IDA* panel, run search. Verify heuristic actually used matches selection, not JPS panel.\n13\t\n14\t## Priority 2 — No \"path not found\" feedback\n15\t\n16\t**File:** `visual/js/view.js:245`\n17\t**Scenario:** Surround start node with walls. Run any algorithm. Verify user gets clear \"No path found\" message instead of silent finish with `length: 0`.\n18\t\n19\t## Priority 3 — Start equals end\n20\t\n21\t**Scenario:** Drag end node onto start node position. Run search. Verify no crash, graceful zero-length path or no-op.\n22\t\n23\t## Priority 4 — Drag start/end during search\n24\t\n25\t**Scenario:** Begin search, attempt to drag start/end while animating. Verify state machine blocks drag (only allowed in `ready`/`finished` states). No crash or state corruption.\n26\t\n27\t## Priority 5 — Wall on start or end position\n28\t\n29\t**Scenario:** Place wall on start node position. Run search. Expect graceful failure, not crash.\n30\t\n31\t## Priority 6 — Pause / Resume cycle\n32\t\n33\t**Scenario:** Start search, pause mid-animation, resume. Verify animation continues from exact paused state with no duplicate or skipped operations.\n34\t\n35\t## Priority 7 — Restart during search\n36\t\n37\t**Scenario:** Start search, click Restart before finish. Verify animation clears, new search begins cleanly, no stale colored nodes remain.\n38\t\n39\t## Priority 8 — JPS diagonal modes not selectable\n40\t\n41\t**Gap:** Only 2 of 4 JumpPointFinder diagonal modes exposed in UI. `Always` and `OnlyWhenNoObstacles` missing.\n42\t**Scenario:** Document what UI changes needed; build scenario that exercises all 4 modes if dropdown were added.\n43\t\n44\t## Priority 9 — Bi-directional vs unidirectional comparison\n45\t\n46\t**Scenario:** Same grid, run A* unidirectional then bi-directional. Verify bi-directional explores fewer nodes; same or similar path.\n47\t\n48\t## Priority 10 — Weight parameter effect\n49\t\n50\t**Scenario:** Run A* with weight=1 vs weight=5 on same grid. Higher weight → fewer operations (greedier) but potentially longer path.\n51\t\n52\t## Priority 11 — IDA* time limit\n53\t\n54\t**Scenario:** Dense wall grid, set time limit to 1ms, run IDA*. Verify IDA* aborts at time limit with some feedback.\n55\t\n56\t## Priority 12 — Full grid walls\n57\t\n58\t**Scenario:** Draw walls everywhere. Run search. Verify robust no-path handling, no JS errors.\n59\t\n60\t## Priority 13 — Large operation count performance\n61\t\n62\t**Scenario:** Dijkstra or BFS on open 64x36 grid, start top-left, end bottom-right. Verify animation remains smooth at 300 ops/sec.\n63\t\n64\t## Priority 14 — Adjacent start/end\n65\t\n66\t**Scenario:** Start and end nodes 1 step apart. Verify minimal animation, path length ~1, fast finish.\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fdbe8a25-98f6-47c1-a871-b0add9ba0ea4","uuid":"4ae5c367-63d6-4ae8-b2d1-ff72c1f8b163","timestamp":"2026-04-16T14:04:38.456Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/sagar/template-repo/docs/experiments/001-demo-artifacts/fleets/fleet-01-test-blitz/workers/scenario-builder/input/assignments.md","content":"# Scenario Builder — Visual & UI Test Scenarios\n\n## Scope\nBuild test scenarios for the visual demo app based on gaps identified in the visual audit.\n\n---\n\n## Priority 1 — Bug: IDA* heuristic reads wrong radio group\n\n**File:** `visual/js/panel.js:160`\n**Bug:** Reads `input[name=jump_point_heuristic]` instead of `input[name=ida_heuristic]`\n**Scenario:** Select IDA*, pick Euclidean in IDA* panel, run search. Verify heuristic actually used matches selection, not JPS panel.\n\n## Priority 2 — No \"path not found\" feedback\n\n**File:** `visual/js/view.js:245`\n**Scenario:** Surround start node with walls. Run any algorithm. Verify user gets clear \"No path found\" message instead of silent finish with `length: 0`.\n\n## Priority 3 — Start equals end\n\n**Scenario:** Drag end node onto start node position. Run search. Verify no crash, graceful zero-length path or no-op.\n\n## Priority 4 — Drag start/end during search\n\n**Scenario:** Begin search, attempt to drag start/end while animating. Verify state machine blocks drag (only allowed in `ready`/`finished` states). No crash or state corruption.\n\n## Priority 5 — Wall on start or end position\n\n**Scenario:** Place wall on start node position. Run search. Expect graceful failure, not crash.\n\n## Priority 6 — Pause / Resume cycle\n\n**Scenario:** Start search, pause mid-animation, resume. Verify animation continues from exact paused state with no duplicate or skipped operations.\n\n## Priority 7 — Restart during search\n\n**Scenario:** Start search, click Restart before finish. Verify animation clears, new search begins cleanly, no stale colored nodes remain.\n\n## Priority 8 — JPS diagonal modes not selectable\n\n**Gap:** Only 2 of 4 JumpPointFinder diagonal modes exposed in UI. `Always` and `OnlyWhenNoObstacles` missing.\n**Scenario:** Document what UI changes needed; build scenario that exercises all 4 modes if dropdown were added.\n\n## Priority 9 — Bi-directional vs unidirectional comparison\n\n**Scenario:** Same grid, run A* unidirectional then bi-directional. Verify bi-directional explores fewer nodes; same or similar path.\n\n## Priority 10 — Weight parameter effect\n\n**Scenario:** Run A* with weight=1 vs weight=5 on same grid. Higher weight → fewer operations (greedier) but potentially longer path.\n\n## Priority 11 — IDA* time limit\n\n**Scenario:** Dense wall grid, set time limit to 1ms, run IDA*. Verify IDA* aborts at time limit with some feedback.\n\n## Priority 12 — Full grid walls\n\n**Scenario:** Draw walls everywhere. Run search. Verify robust no-path handling, no JS errors.\n\n## Priority 13 — Large operation count performance\n\n**Scenario:** Dijkstra or BFS on open 64x36 grid, start top-left, end bottom-right. Verify animation remains smooth at 300 ops/sec.\n\n## Priority 14 — Adjacent start/end\n\n**Scenario:** Start and end nodes 1 step apart. Verify minimal animation, path length ~1, fast finish.\n","numLines":67,"startLine":1,"totalLines":67}}}
