{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CwHyT5xr81PoLjkCcNnJ8i","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/**\n2\t * Backtrace according to the parent records and return the path.\n3\t * (including both start and end nodes)\n4\t * @param {Node} node End node\n5\t * @return {Array<Array<number>>} the path\n6\t */\n7\tfunction backtrace(node) {\n8\t    var path = [[node.x, node.y]];\n9\t    while (node.parent) {\n10\t        node = node.parent;\n11\t        path.push([node.x, node.y]);\n12\t    }\n13\t    return path.reverse();\n14\t}\n15\texports.backtrace = backtrace;\n16\t\n17\t/**\n18\t * Backtrace from start and end node, and return the path.\n19\t * (including both start and end nodes)\n20\t * @param {Node}\n21\t * @param {Node}\n22\t */\n23\tfunction biBacktrace(nodeA, nodeB) {\n24\t    var pathA = backtrace(nodeA),\n25\t        pathB = backtrace(nodeB);\n26\t    return pathA.concat(pathB.reverse());\n27\t}\n28\texports.biBacktrace = biBacktrace;\n29\t\n30\t/**\n31\t * Compute the length of the path.\n32\t * @param {Array<Array<number>>} path The path\n33\t * @return {number} The length of the path\n34\t */\n35\tfunction pathLength(path) {\n36\t    var i, sum = 0, a, b, dx, dy;\n37\t    for (i = 1; i < path.length; ++i) {\n38\t        a = path[i - 1];\n39\t        b = path[i];\n40\t        dx = a[0] - b[0];\n41\t        dy = a[1] - b[1];\n42\t        sum += Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy);\n43\t    }\n44\t    return sum;\n45\t}\n46\texports.pathLength = pathLength;\n47\t\n48\t\n49\t/**\n50\t * Given the start and end coordinates, return all the coordinates lying\n51\t * on the line formed by these coordinates, based on Bresenham's algorithm.\n52\t * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bresenham's_line_algorithm#Simplification\n53\t * @param {number} x0 Start x coordinate\n54\t * @param {number} y0 Start y coordinate\n55\t * @param {number} x1 End x coordinate\n56\t * @param {number} y1 End y coordinate\n57\t * @return {Array<Array<number>>} The coordinates on the line\n58\t */\n59\tfunction interpolate(x0, y0, x1, y1) {\n60\t    var abs = Math.abs,\n61\t        line = [],\n62\t        sx, sy, dx, dy, err, e2;\n63\t\n64\t    dx = abs(x1 - x0);\n65\t    dy = abs(y1 - y0);\n66\t\n67\t    sx = (x0 < x1) ? 1 : -1;\n68\t    sy = (y0 < y1) ? 1 : -1;\n69\t\n70\t    err = dx - dy;\n71\t\n72\t    while (true) {\n73\t        line.push([x0, y0]);\n74\t\n75\t        if (x0 === x1 && y0 === y1) {\n76\t            break;\n77\t        }\n78\t        \n79\t        e2 = 2 * err;\n80\t        if (e2 > -dy) {\n81\t            err = err - dy;\n82\t            x0 = x0 + sx;\n83\t        }\n84\t        if (e2 < dx) {\n85\t            err = err + dx;\n86\t            y0 = y0 + sy;\n87\t        }\n88\t    }\n89\t\n90\t    return line;\n91\t}\n92\texports.interpolate = interpolate;\n93\t\n94\t\n95\t/**\n96\t * Given a compressed path, return a new path that has all the segments\n97\t * in it interpolated.\n98\t * @param {Array<Array<number>>} path The path\n99\t * @return {Array<Array<number>>} expanded path\n100\t */\n101\tfunction expandPath(path) {\n102\t    var expanded = [],\n103\t        len = path.length,\n104\t        coord0, coord1,\n105\t        interpolated,\n106\t        interpolatedLen,\n107\t        i, j;\n108\t\n109\t    if (len < 2) {\n110\t        return expanded;\n111\t    }\n112\t\n113\t    for (i = 0; i < len - 1; ++i) {\n114\t        coord0 = path[i];\n115\t        coord1 = path[i + 1];\n116\t\n117\t        interpolated = interpolate(coord0[0], coord0[1], coord1[0], coord1[1]);\n118\t        interpolatedLen = interpolated.length;\n119\t        for (j = 0; j < interpolatedLen - 1; ++j) {\n120\t            expanded.push(interpolated[j]);\n121\t        }\n122\t    }\n123\t    expanded.push(path[len - 1]);\n124\t\n125\t    return expanded;\n126\t}\n127\texports.expandPath = expandPath;\n128\t\n129\t\n130\t/**\n131\t * Smoothen the give path.\n132\t * The original path will not be modified; a new path will be returned.\n133\t * @param {PF.Grid} grid\n134\t * @param {Array<Array<number>>} path The path\n135\t */\n136\tfunction smoothenPath(grid, path) {\n137\t    var len = path.length,\n138\t        x0 = path[0][0],        // path start x\n139\t        y0 = path[0][1],        // path start y\n140\t        x1 = path[len - 1][0],  // path end x\n141\t        y1 = path[len - 1][1],  // path end y\n142\t        sx, sy,                 // current start coordinate\n143\t        ex, ey,                 // current end coordinate\n144\t        newPath,\n145\t        i, j, coord, line, testCoord, blocked;\n146\t\n147\t    sx = x0;\n148\t    sy = y0;\n149\t    newPath = [[sx, sy]];\n150\t\n151\t    for (i = 2; i < len; ++i) {\n152\t        coord = path[i];\n153\t        ex = coord[0];\n154\t        ey = coord[1];\n155\t        line = interpolate(sx, sy, ex, ey);\n156\t\n157\t        blocked = false;\n158\t        for (j = 1; j < line.length; ++j) {\n159\t            testCoord = line[j];\n160\t\n161\t            if (!grid.isWalkableAt(testCoord[0], testCoord[1])) {\n162\t                blocked = true;\n163\t                break;\n164\t            }\n165\t        }\n166\t        if (blocked) {\n167\t            lastValidCoord = path[i - 1];\n168\t            newPath.push(lastValidCoord);\n169\t            sx = lastValidCoord[0];\n170\t            sy = lastValidCoord[1];\n171\t        }\n172\t    }\n173\t    newPath.push([x1, y1]);\n174\t\n175\t    return newPath;\n176\t}\n177\texports.smoothenPath = smoothenPath;\n178\t\n179\t\n180\t/**\n181\t * Compress a path, remove redundant nodes without altering the shape\n182\t * The original path is not modified\n183\t * @param {Array<Array<number>>} path The path\n184\t * @return {Array<Array<number>>} The compressed path\n185\t */\n186\tfunction compressPath(path) {\n187\t\n188\t    // nothing to compress\n189\t    if(path.length < 3) {\n190\t        return path;\n191\t    }\n192\t\n193\t    var compressed = [],\n194\t        sx = path[0][0], // start x\n195\t        sy = path[0][1], // start y\n196\t        px = path[1][0], // second point x\n197\t        py = path[1][1], // second point y\n198\t        dx = px - sx, // direction between the two points\n199\t        dy = py - sy, // direction between the two points\n200\t        lx, ly,\n201\t        ldx, ldy,\n202\t        sq, i;\n203\t\n204\t    // normalize the direction\n205\t    sq = Math.sqrt(dx*dx + dy*dy);\n206\t    dx /= sq;\n207\t    dy /= sq;\n208\t\n209\t    // start the new path\n210\t    compressed.push([sx,sy]);\n211\t\n212\t    for(i = 2; i < path.length; i++) {\n213\t\n214\t        // store the last point\n215\t        lx = px;\n216\t        ly = py;\n217\t\n218\t        // store the last direction\n219\t        ldx = dx;\n220\t        ldy = dy;\n221\t\n222\t        // next point\n223\t        px = path[i][0];\n224\t        py = path[i][1];\n225\t\n226\t        // next direction\n227\t        dx = px - lx;\n228\t        dy = py - ly;\n229\t\n230\t        // normalize\n231\t        sq = Math.sqrt(dx*dx + dy*dy);\n232\t        dx /= sq;\n233\t        dy /= sq;\n234\t\n235\t        // if the direction has changed, store the point\n236\t        if ( dx !== ldx || dy !== ldy ) {\n237\t            compressed.push([lx,ly]);\n238\t        }\n239\t    }\n240\t\n241\t    // store the last point\n242\t    compressed.push([px,py]);\n243\t\n244\t    return compressed;\n245\t}\n246\texports.compressPath = compressPath;\n247\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fdbe8a25-98f6-47c1-a871-b0add9ba0ea4","uuid":"377efe2d-694e-4ec4-a259-f5a0e5135e31","timestamp":"2026-04-16T14:05:01.236Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/sagar/template-repo/src/core/Util.js","content":"/**\n * Backtrace according to the parent records and return the path.\n * (including both start and end nodes)\n * @param {Node} node End node\n * @return {Array<Array<number>>} the path\n */\nfunction backtrace(node) {\n    var path = [[node.x, node.y]];\n    while (node.parent) {\n        node = node.parent;\n        path.push([node.x, node.y]);\n    }\n    return path.reverse();\n}\nexports.backtrace = backtrace;\n\n/**\n * Backtrace from start and end node, and return the path.\n * (including both start and end nodes)\n * @param {Node}\n * @param {Node}\n */\nfunction biBacktrace(nodeA, nodeB) {\n    var pathA = backtrace(nodeA),\n        pathB = backtrace(nodeB);\n    return pathA.concat(pathB.reverse());\n}\nexports.biBacktrace = biBacktrace;\n\n/**\n * Compute the length of the path.\n * @param {Array<Array<number>>} path The path\n * @return {number} The length of the path\n */\nfunction pathLength(path) {\n    var i, sum = 0, a, b, dx, dy;\n    for (i = 1; i < path.length; ++i) {\n        a = path[i - 1];\n        b = path[i];\n        dx = a[0] - b[0];\n        dy = a[1] - b[1];\n        sum += Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy);\n    }\n    return sum;\n}\nexports.pathLength = pathLength;\n\n\n/**\n * Given the start and end coordinates, return all the coordinates lying\n * on the line formed by these coordinates, based on Bresenham's algorithm.\n * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bresenham's_line_algorithm#Simplification\n * @param {number} x0 Start x coordinate\n * @param {number} y0 Start y coordinate\n * @param {number} x1 End x coordinate\n * @param {number} y1 End y coordinate\n * @return {Array<Array<number>>} The coordinates on the line\n */\nfunction interpolate(x0, y0, x1, y1) {\n    var abs = Math.abs,\n        line = [],\n        sx, sy, dx, dy, err, e2;\n\n    dx = abs(x1 - x0);\n    dy = abs(y1 - y0);\n\n    sx = (x0 < x1) ? 1 : -1;\n    sy = (y0 < y1) ? 1 : -1;\n\n    err = dx - dy;\n\n    while (true) {\n        line.push([x0, y0]);\n\n        if (x0 === x1 && y0 === y1) {\n            break;\n        }\n        \n        e2 = 2 * err;\n        if (e2 > -dy) {\n            err = err - dy;\n            x0 = x0 + sx;\n        }\n        if (e2 < dx) {\n            err = err + dx;\n            y0 = y0 + sy;\n        }\n    }\n\n    return line;\n}\nexports.interpolate = interpolate;\n\n\n/**\n * Given a compressed path, return a new path that has all the segments\n * in it interpolated.\n * @param {Array<Array<number>>} path The path\n * @return {Array<Array<number>>} expanded path\n */\nfunction expandPath(path) {\n    var expanded = [],\n        len = path.length,\n        coord0, coord1,\n        interpolated,\n        interpolatedLen,\n        i, j;\n\n    if (len < 2) {\n        return expanded;\n    }\n\n    for (i = 0; i < len - 1; ++i) {\n        coord0 = path[i];\n        coord1 = path[i + 1];\n\n        interpolated = interpolate(coord0[0], coord0[1], coord1[0], coord1[1]);\n        interpolatedLen = interpolated.length;\n        for (j = 0; j < interpolatedLen - 1; ++j) {\n            expanded.push(interpolated[j]);\n        }\n    }\n    expanded.push(path[len - 1]);\n\n    return expanded;\n}\nexports.expandPath = expandPath;\n\n\n/**\n * Smoothen the give path.\n * The original path will not be modified; a new path will be returned.\n * @param {PF.Grid} grid\n * @param {Array<Array<number>>} path The path\n */\nfunction smoothenPath(grid, path) {\n    var len = path.length,\n        x0 = path[0][0],        // path start x\n        y0 = path[0][1],        // path start y\n        x1 = path[len - 1][0],  // path end x\n        y1 = path[len - 1][1],  // path end y\n        sx, sy,                 // current start coordinate\n        ex, ey,                 // current end coordinate\n        newPath,\n        i, j, coord, line, testCoord, blocked;\n\n    sx = x0;\n    sy = y0;\n    newPath = [[sx, sy]];\n\n    for (i = 2; i < len; ++i) {\n        coord = path[i];\n        ex = coord[0];\n        ey = coord[1];\n        line = interpolate(sx, sy, ex, ey);\n\n        blocked = false;\n        for (j = 1; j < line.length; ++j) {\n            testCoord = line[j];\n\n            if (!grid.isWalkableAt(testCoord[0], testCoord[1])) {\n                blocked = true;\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n        if (blocked) {\n            lastValidCoord = path[i - 1];\n            newPath.push(lastValidCoord);\n            sx = lastValidCoord[0];\n            sy = lastValidCoord[1];\n        }\n    }\n    newPath.push([x1, y1]);\n\n    return newPath;\n}\nexports.smoothenPath = smoothenPath;\n\n\n/**\n * Compress a path, remove redundant nodes without altering the shape\n * The original path is not modified\n * @param {Array<Array<number>>} path The path\n * @return {Array<Array<number>>} The compressed path\n */\nfunction compressPath(path) {\n\n    // nothing to compress\n    if(path.length < 3) {\n        return path;\n    }\n\n    var compressed = [],\n        sx = path[0][0], // start x\n        sy = path[0][1], // start y\n        px = path[1][0], // second point x\n        py = path[1][1], // second point y\n        dx = px - sx, // direction between the two points\n        dy = py - sy, // direction between the two points\n        lx, ly,\n        ldx, ldy,\n        sq, i;\n\n    // normalize the direction\n    sq = Math.sqrt(dx*dx + dy*dy);\n    dx /= sq;\n    dy /= sq;\n\n    // start the new path\n    compressed.push([sx,sy]);\n\n    for(i = 2; i < path.length; i++) {\n\n        // store the last point\n        lx = px;\n        ly = py;\n\n        // store the last direction\n        ldx = dx;\n        ldy = dy;\n\n        // next point\n        px = path[i][0];\n        py = path[i][1];\n\n        // next direction\n        dx = px - lx;\n        dy = py - ly;\n\n        // normalize\n        sq = Math.sqrt(dx*dx + dy*dy);\n        dx /= sq;\n        dy /= sq;\n\n        // if the direction has changed, store the point\n        if ( dx !== ldx || dy !== ldy ) {\n            compressed.push([lx,ly]);\n        }\n    }\n\n    // store the last point\n    compressed.push([px,py]);\n\n    return compressed;\n}\nexports.compressPath = compressPath;\n","numLines":247,"startLine":1,"totalLines":247}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_014wM6weWxq8pqbGbZ29ocAN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a good understanding of the codebase. Let me build the test scenarios. I need to create tests in the `test/` directory and potentially fix the IDA* heuristic bug in `visual/js/panel.js`.\n\nLet me plan the work:\n\n1. **Priority 1 - IDA* heuristic bug**: Line 160 reads `jump_point_heuristic` instead of `ida_heuristic`. This is a UI bug in the visual app. I can write a test for the underlying IDA* finder behavior with different heuristics, and document the UI bug fix.\n\n\n2. **Priority 2 - No \"path not found\" feedback**: When path is empty, `view.js:drawPath` just returns silently. Need to test that finders return empty path when no path exists.\n3. **Priority 3 - Start equals end**: Test that finders handle start==end gracefully.\n4. **Priority 4 - Drag during search**: State machine test - dragStart/dragEnd only allowed from ready/finished states.\n5. **Priority 5 - Wall on start/end**: Test finder behavior when start/end is blocked.\n6. **Priority 6 - Pause/Resume**: State machine transitions test.\n7. **Priority 7 - Restart during search**: State machine test.\n8. **Priority 8 - J**: (appears to be cut off, but likely another state machine or edge case test)\n9. **Priority 9 - Diagonal modes**: Document and test all 4 diagonal modes.\n10. **Priority 10 - Bi-directional comparison**: Compare node exploration counts.\n11. **Priority 11 - Weight parameter**: Test weight effect on A*.\n12. **Priority 12 - IDA* time limit**: Test time limit behavior.\n13. **Priority 13 - Full grid walls**: All walls, no path possible.\n14. **Priority 14 - Large operation count**: Performance test on open grid.\n15. **Priority 15 - Adjacent start/end**: Minimal path test.\n\nSince these are backend library tests and the visual app relies on jQuery/DOM which can't be tested in Node, I'll focus on the pathfinding library behavior for these scenarios. For UI-specific items like state machine and drag behavior, I'll document what needs testing but acknowledge I can't unit test without a browser environment. Now I'll create the test file and address the bug.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6032,"cache_read_input_tokens":40737,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6032},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fdbe8a25-98f6-47c1-a871-b0add9ba0ea4","uuid":"f9418455-2ee2-4339-85b1-8547c59ac455"}
