{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Q1Jbgq9LYH2WvBYW5s8gFT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016ugKGiqxyYhJuHWwR1xUZG","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/sagar/template-repo/docs/experiments/001-demo-artifacts/fleets/fleet-01-test-blitz/workers/scenario-builder/output/summary.md","content":"# Scenario Builder — Summary\n\n## Bug Fix\n\n### Priority 1 — IDA* heuristic reads wrong radio group\n- **File:** `visual/js/panel.js:160`\n- **Fix:** Changed `$('input[name=jump_point_heuristic]:checked')` → `$('input[name=ida_heuristic]:checked')`\n- **Impact:** IDA* panel was reading JPS heuristic radio group instead of its own. User-selected heuristic in IDA* section was ignored.\n\n## Test Scenarios Created\n\n**File:** `test/VisualScenarios.js` — 39 tests across 14 priority scenarios.\n\n| Priority | Scenario | Tests | Status |\n|----------|----------|-------|--------|\n| 1 | IDA* heuristic independence | 2 | ✅ Pass |\n| 2 | No path found (start surrounded) | 4 | ✅ Pass |\n| 3 | Start equals end | 5 | ✅ Pass |\n| 4 | Drag during search (state machine) | 1 | ✅ Documented |\n| 5 | Wall on start/end position | 4 | ✅ Pass |\n| 6 | Pause/Resume cycle | 1 | ✅ Documented |\n| 7 | Restart during search | 1 | ✅ Documented |\n| 8 | JPS all 4 diagonal modes | 4 | ✅ Pass |\n| 9 | Bi-directional vs unidirectional | 1 | ✅ Pass |\n| 10 | Weight parameter effect | 1 | ✅ Pass |\n| 11 | IDA* time limit | 3 | ✅ Pass |\n| 12 | Full grid walls | 3 | ✅ Pass |\n| 13 | Large grid performance (64×36) | 2 | ✅ Pass |\n| 14 | Adjacent start/end | 4 | ✅ Pass |\n\n## Key Findings\n\n1. **Finders don't validate start/end walkability.** They push start into open list unconditionally. Visual app handles this via `isStartOrEndPos` guard in `mousedown` handler.\n\n2. **JPS UI gap confirmed.** Only `IfAtMostOneObstacle` and `Never` exposed. `Always` and `OnlyWhenNoObstacles` work at library level but need UI dropdown to be selectable. Panel.js hardcodes `DiagonalMovement.IfAtMostOneObstacle` at line 139.\n\n3. **State machine correctly guards drag.** `dragStart`/`dragEnd` only allowed from `ready`/`finished` states. No drag possible during `searching`/`paused`.\n\n4. **Pause/resume is clean.** `loop()` checks `Controller.is('searching')` — pausing stops the loop, resume re-enters it from same operations array position.\n\n5. **No \"path not found\" UI feedback.** `view.js:drawPath` returns silently on empty path. `showStats` shows `length: 0` but no explicit message. This is a UI gap, not a library bug.\n\n## Full Suite Result\n\n```\n256 passing (1s)\n0 failing\n```\n\nNo regressions introduced.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":846,"cache_read_input_tokens":68727,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":846},"output_tokens":53,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fdbe8a25-98f6-47c1-a871-b0add9ba0ea4","uuid":"9c9b663c-0e82-42a5-9551-14e2d614081e"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016ugKGiqxyYhJuHWwR1xUZG","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /home/sagar/template-repo/docs/experiments/001-demo-artifacts/fleets/fleet-01-test-blitz/workers/scenario-builder/output/summary.md"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fdbe8a25-98f6-47c1-a871-b0add9ba0ea4","uuid":"f58b8def-5a6a-486c-82d1-286015801374","timestamp":"2026-04-16T14:09:03.846Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/home/sagar/template-repo/docs/experiments/001-demo-artifacts/fleets/fleet-01-test-blitz/workers/scenario-builder/output/summary.md","content":"# Scenario Builder — Summary\n\n## Bug Fix\n\n### Priority 1 — IDA* heuristic reads wrong radio group\n- **File:** `visual/js/panel.js:160`\n- **Fix:** Changed `$('input[name=jump_point_heuristic]:checked')` → `$('input[name=ida_heuristic]:checked')`\n- **Impact:** IDA* panel was reading JPS heuristic radio group instead of its own. User-selected heuristic in IDA* section was ignored.\n\n## Test Scenarios Created\n\n**File:** `test/VisualScenarios.js` — 39 tests across 14 priority scenarios.\n\n| Priority | Scenario | Tests | Status |\n|----------|----------|-------|--------|\n| 1 | IDA* heuristic independence | 2 | ✅ Pass |\n| 2 | No path found (start surrounded) | 4 | ✅ Pass |\n| 3 | Start equals end | 5 | ✅ Pass |\n| 4 | Drag during search (state machine) | 1 | ✅ Documented |\n| 5 | Wall on start/end position | 4 | ✅ Pass |\n| 6 | Pause/Resume cycle | 1 | ✅ Documented |\n| 7 | Restart during search | 1 | ✅ Documented |\n| 8 | JPS all 4 diagonal modes | 4 | ✅ Pass |\n| 9 | Bi-directional vs unidirectional | 1 | ✅ Pass |\n| 10 | Weight parameter effect | 1 | ✅ Pass |\n| 11 | IDA* time limit | 3 | ✅ Pass |\n| 12 | Full grid walls | 3 | ✅ Pass |\n| 13 | Large grid performance (64×36) | 2 | ✅ Pass |\n| 14 | Adjacent start/end | 4 | ✅ Pass |\n\n## Key Findings\n\n1. **Finders don't validate start/end walkability.** They push start into open list unconditionally. Visual app handles this via `isStartOrEndPos` guard in `mousedown` handler.\n\n2. **JPS UI gap confirmed.** Only `IfAtMostOneObstacle` and `Never` exposed. `Always` and `OnlyWhenNoObstacles` work at library level but need UI dropdown to be selectable. Panel.js hardcodes `DiagonalMovement.IfAtMostOneObstacle` at line 139.\n\n3. **State machine correctly guards drag.** `dragStart`/`dragEnd` only allowed from `ready`/`finished` states. No drag possible during `searching`/`paused`.\n\n4. **Pause/resume is clean.** `loop()` checks `Controller.is('searching')` — pausing stops the loop, resume re-enters it from same operations array position.\n\n5. **No \"path not found\" UI feedback.** `view.js:drawPath` returns silently on empty path. `showStats` shows `length: 0` but no explicit message. This is a UI gap, not a library bug.\n\n## Full Suite Result\n\n```\n256 passing (1s)\n0 failing\n```\n\nNo regressions introduced.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
